{"agent_id":"pp3g-Mjzt-research-read-only-investigate-crosslink-s-hook-d493","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T02:32:22.520156051Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6ba05875-831a-4fb5-bad1-fad45f03864d","comment_uuid":"d59d7f8a-4088-4d92-8079-be5842229ee8","author":"pp3g-Mjzt-research-read-only-investigate-crosslink-s-hook-d493","content":"RESULT: Crosslink hook system — full enumeration, interception points, and doc-check hook recommendation\n\n## 1. Hook events and payloads\n\n### Claude Code hooks (official docs reference; this repo's .claude/settings.json uses command hooks)\nCommon input fields (JSON on stdin): session_id, prompt_id, transcript_path, cwd, permission_mode, effort, hook_event_name; subagents add agent_id + agent_type.\n\n- SessionStart (matcher startup|resume) / SessionEnd\n- UserPromptSubmit (input.prompt) / UserPromptExpansion\n- Stop / StopFailure\n- PreToolUse — input: tool_name, tool_input, tool_use_id. Decision via hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision: allow|deny|ask|defer, plus updatedInput (replace tool input) and additionalContext (inject text into Claude's context). Exit 2 == deny. Precedence deny > defer > ask > allow.\n  - Bash tool_input: {command, description, timeout, run_in_background}\n  - Write: {file_path (absolute), content}; Edit: {file_path, old_string, new_string, replace_all}\n- PostToolUse / PostToolUseFailure / PostToolBatch — input: tool_name, tool_input, tool_response\n- SubagentStart / SubagentStop (TaskCreated/TaskCompleted)\n- PreCompact / PostCompact\n- Notification\n- ConfigChange — input: source (user_settings|project_settings|local_settings|policy_settings|skills), file_path. Fires AFTER a settings/skill file changes; decision block prevents the change from applying. NOT a pre-check.\n- TeammateIdle, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, CwdChanged, FileChanged, DirectoryAdded, MessageDisplay, PermissionRequest, Elicitation\n\n### OpenCode plugin hooks (@opencode-ai/plugin v1.17.9, exact signatures in ~/.config/opencode/node_modules/@opencode-ai/plugin/dist/index.d.ts)\n- chat.message {sessionID, agent, model, messageID, variant}\n- chat.params {sessionID, agent, model, provider, message} → temperature/topP/topK/maxOutputTokens/options\n- chat.headers\n- permission.ask (Permission) → status ask|deny|allow\n- command.execute.before {command, sessionID, arguments} → parts (fires for slash commands, NOT for Bash tool calls)\n- tool.execute.before {tool, sessionID, callID} → args (mutable; for bash, output.args.command is the command string)\n- shell.env {cwd, sessionID, callID}\n- tool.execute.after {tool, sessionID, callID, args} → title/output/metadata\n- experimental.chat.messages.transform / system.transform / session.compacting / compaction.autocontinue / text.complete / provider.small_model\n\n## 2. Where hooks are configured\n- .claude/settings.json — Claude Code hook registration. This repo: PreToolUse Write|Edit|Bash → work-check.py; WebFetch|WebSearch → pre-web-check.py; PostToolUse Write|Edit → post-edit-check.py + heartbeat.py; SessionStart → session-start.py; UserPromptSubmit → prompt-guard.py. Commands resolve via $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.claude/hooks/*.py with a [ -f ] guard (missing script = silent no-op).\n- .claude/hooks/ — main repo has 7 scripts (crosslink_config.py, heartbeat.py, post-edit-check.py, pre-web-check.py, prompt-guard.py, session-start.py, work-check.py). Worktrees get ONLY crosslink_config.py + heartbeat.py (launch.rs ensure_worktree_hooks writes those two; the rest silently no-op via the [ -f ] guard).\n- .opencode/opencode.json — plugin array: orchestrator-guard.ts, crosslink-guard.ts, rtk-guard.ts.\n- .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts — native TS replication of work-check.py: tool.execute.before on write/edit/bash, loads .crosslink/hook-config.json + .crosslink/hook-config.local.json, per-session agent-type tracking via chat.params/chat.message.\n- .crosslink/hook-config.json — guard config (blocked/gated git, allowed_bash_prefixes, by_type overrides, comment_discipline, agent.type/phase_types, kickoff.allowed_tools, sandbox.command). This is CONFIG for the guards, not a hook registration surface itself.\n- Canonical templates: crosslink crate resources/claude/settings.json + resources/claude/hooks/*.py, embedded via include_str! in crosslink/src/commands/init/mod.rs, deployed by crosslink init.\n\n## 3. Can a hook fire BEFORE kickoff/swarm dispatch or hook-config.json edits?\nYES for agent-invoked dispatch — with one hard limitation.\n\n- crosslink kickoff run / crosslink swarm launch are Bash tool calls in the PARENT session. OpenCode tool.execute.before (tool=bash) fires before execution: the plugin sees output.args.command = 'crosslink kickoff run ...' and can THROW to block or MUTATE the command (rtk-guard.ts precedent: output.args.command = 'rtk read <doc> && crosslink kickoff run ...'). Claude Code PreToolUse matcher Bash sees tool_input.command and can exit 2 (block) or return additionalContext.\n- The crosslink CLI itself has NO pre-dispatch hookpoint: kickoff/run.rs + launch.rs + swarm/lifecycle.rs spawn the child (tmux + build_agent_command) without invoking any hook. The child session's hooks (heartbeat etc.) run only AFTER launch.\n- command.execute.before does NOT fire for crosslink CLI — it fires for opencode slash commands only. tool.execute.before is the correct interception.\n- hook-config.json edits: OpenCode tool.execute.before on write/edit (output.args.filePath) and Claude Code PreToolUse Write|Edit (tool_input.file_path, absolute) both fire BEFORE the write. ConfigChange is NOT usable as a pre-check (fires after, and only for Claude settings/skills files, not hook-config.json).\n- HARD LIMITATION: hooks fire only inside an agent session. A human running crosslink kickoff run in a terminal is intercepted by nothing — only a shell wrapper or a change inside the crosslink CLI itself could catch that.\n\n## 4. Recommendation — where a doc-check hook should live\nPrimary (recommended): extend .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts (or add .opencode/plugins/doc-check-guard.ts registered in .opencode/opencode.json) with tool.execute.before:\n- bash: if output.args.command matches /crosslink (kickoff run|swarm launch|session start|quick)/ → require the doc/knowledge page read first: either throw with 'read <path> first' or prepend 'rtk read <path> && ' to the command (mutation proven by rtk-guard.ts).\n- write/edit: if output.args.filePath ends with .crosslink/hook-config.json or .crosslink/hook-config.local.json → same doc gate.\nWhy plugin-first: .opencode/plugins/ ships with the branch into worktrees (only .opencode/agents/*.md are copied from root; plugins come from the branch), so the guard is present in every agent session without touching launch.rs.\n\nClaude Code counterpart (optional, for claude-binary sessions): add a PreToolUse matcher Bash + Write|Edit entry in .claude/settings.json pointing to a new .claude/hooks/doc-check.py (pattern: work-check.py reads tool_input.command / tool_input.file_path). Caveat: worktree .claude/hooks/ only carries crosslink_config.py + heartbeat.py, so the new script must be added to launch.rs ensure_worktree_hooks or the [ -f ] guard will silently skip it in worktrees.\n\nInjection capability: block-and-instruct (throw/exit 2 with stderr message naming the doc) is the reliable mechanism; command mutation (prepend rtk read) is proven but changes the command the agent sees; additionalContext (Claude Code) injects doc text into the parent's context. None of these can inject into the CHILD agent's context before launch — the child must be instructed to read the doc itself.\n\nEvidence files: .claude/settings.json, .claude/hooks/*.py, .opencode/opencode.json, .opencode/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts, .crosslink/hook-config.json, crosslink crate resources/claude/*, crosslink/src/commands/{init,kickoff,swarm}/*.rs, ~/.config/opencode/node_modules/@opencode-ai/plugin/dist/index.d.ts, official Claude Code hooks reference (tool_012b1f8b4001Y3EwwaPaKPOPeG).","created_at":"2026-08-18T02:32:22.510397937Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:hflk01ZRT+wUSRzfNYVgtQG/oRVwxUxSLdN5MTMzFpA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbDwDwTqKkik2f8/Ypq4MtksQwV91gDZAwxRXXu0bGpsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA5Cre8e1J/ScNh0rRb5k0BXr3XEMUPJudXCGrJ9KNlKiKBnP6EQsgu7zgApz4Aq59zsT0pvI9Db72tkdWedEeCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hflk01ZRT+wUSRzfNYVgtQG/oRVwxUxSLdN5MTMzFpA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbDwDwTqKkik2f8/Ypq4MtksQwV91gDZAwxRXXu0bGpsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE7JZuTovA8hdIj4TIUIjIoKNKVd1VwFT7Be8Fzsm4HRe7cBl4Ug9bL4FHfVuVUJyTcslafIsIRZaPWeoZpIww0="}
